<title>FRANCE: Algeria and Libya set up joint investment firm.</title>
<headline>Algeria and Libya set up joint investment firm.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arab Libyan Overseas Investment company and Algerian investors have set up a joint investment firm, named Lafico Algeria Holding, the Algerian official news agency APS said on Monday.</p>
<p>The $8.0 million equity joint venture will deal in financial and real estate business and will buy holdings in financial companies in Algeria and abroad.</p>
<p>The company is based in Algiers, added APS without giving further details.</p>
</text>
